course: dictionary
lesson: 10863
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around it. «Monarch caterpillars eat milkweed, and birds that eat a monarch get sick» is about animals and eating, so the words around the word will show you its meaning.
explain: The sentence says «the viceroy looks very similar and also tastes bad, so they share the warning». Looks similar, tastes bad and share the warning are all clues about animals. So here a viceroy is a butterfly, not a ruler. The check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: In history lessons, a viceroy is a ruler sent far away by a king or queen. The real ruler was far away, and the viceroy ruled in their name. When you meet viceroy, ask: is this a person ruling, or an insect? The clues will tell you.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Viceroy» can mean a person sent to rule a country or colony in a king's or queen's name.
fact: «Viceroy» can also mean an orange North American butterfly that looks like the monarch.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, so always check the clues around them.
exercise: «The viceroy looks very similar and also tastes bad.» What is a viceroy in this sentence? | A type of milkweed | A person who rules a country | A king's castle | *An orange North American butterfly
exercise: In history, what was a viceroy sent to do? | Carry letters to the queen | *Rule a country in the king's or queen's name | Build castles on hills | Catch butterflies for the king
exercise: «Birds that eat a monarch get sick and learn to avoid orange and black butterflies.» Find and copy one word that tells you the viceroy is an animal. | birds | learn | monarch | *butterflies
test: «The viceroy looks very similar to the monarch.» Which clue tells you the viceroy is an insect? | Very similar and also | Looks very similar | *Monarch and butterfly | The word the
test: The Viceroy of India ruled under British rule. What does this tell you about where the real ruler was? | *Far away | Right beside the viceroy | Hiding in the forest | In the same butterfly garden
exam: Ella reads, «The viceroy tastes bad, so birds avoid it.» What does viceroy mean here? | A kind of bird | *An orange butterfly that tastes bad | A person sent to rule a country | A queen's messenger
